Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant tables & columns for the task  
(results and races will be enough – every figure we need ultimately comes from the points column in results)

• results."race_id": link every result to a grand prix (needed to know which season it belongs to).  
• results."driver_id": identify the driver who scored the points so we can total a driver’s points over a season.  
• results."constructor_id": identify the constructor that scored the points so we can total a constructor’s points over a season.  
• results."points": the points to be summed (both for driver totals and constructor totals).  
• races."race_id": join‐key to results.  
• races."year": gives the season / calendar year we finally have to rank by.

Typical conditions that will appear  
• results."points" IS NOT NULL           – ignore NULL point entries.  
• GROUP BY races."year", results."driver_id" (or constructor_id) – to aggregate totals.  
• HAVING MAX(…)                          – to pull out only the best scoring driver / constructor for each season.  
• ORDER BY … LIMIT 3                     – to keep three smallest combined totals.

Ten exploratory SQL queries
All are limited to 20 rows (or fewer) for inspection and are written for SQLite.  
Table / column names are wrapped in double quotes to stay safe.

```sql
-- 1. Peek at the raw results table (first 20 rows)
SELECT *
FROM "results"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2. What seasons exist in the data set? (distinct years via join)
SELECT DISTINCT r."year"
FROM "races" AS r
JOIN "results" AS res ON res."race_id" = r."race_id"
ORDER BY r."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3. Total points per driver in 2009 (sample single season)
SELECT r."year",
       res."driver_id",
       SUM(res."points") AS driver_points
FROM "results" AS res
JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
WHERE r."year" = 2009
GROUP BY r."year", res."driver_id"
ORDER BY driver_points DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4. Highest‑scoring driver for every year (driver max)
SELECT r."year",
       res."driver_id",
       SUM(res."points") AS driver_points
FROM "results" AS res
JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
GROUP BY r."year", res."driver_id"
HAVING driver_points = (
        SELECT MAX(SUM(res2."points"))
        FROM "results" AS res2
        JOIN "races"  AS r2 ON r2."race_id" = res2."race_id"
        WHERE r2."year" = r."year"
        GROUP BY res2."driver_id")
ORDER BY r."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5. Highest‑scoring constructor for every year (constructor max)
SELECT r."year",
       res."constructor_id",
       SUM(res."points") AS constructor_points
FROM "results" AS res
JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
GROUP BY r."year", res."constructor_id"
HAVING constructor_points = (
        SELECT MAX(SUM(res2."points"))
        FROM "results" AS res2
        JOIN "races"  AS r2 ON r2."race_id" = res2."race_id"
        WHERE r2."year" = r."year"
        GROUP BY res2."constructor_id")
ORDER BY r."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6. Combine both maxima for one sample year (e.g., 2009)
WITH driver_max AS (
    SELECT SUM(res."points") AS max_driver_pts
    FROM "results" AS res
    JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
    WHERE r."year" = 2009
    GROUP BY res."driver_id"
    ORDER BY max_driver_pts DESC
    LIMIT 1
),
constructor_max AS (
    SELECT SUM(res."points") AS max_constructor_pts
    FROM "results" AS res
    JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
    WHERE r."year" = 2009
    GROUP BY res."constructor_id"
    ORDER BY max_constructor_pts DESC
    LIMIT 1
)
SELECT (SELECT max_driver_pts FROM driver_max) +
       (SELECT max_constructor_pts FROM constructor_max) AS combined_2009_total;
```

```sql
-- 7. Driver maxima per year (tidy CTE version)
WITH driver_totals AS (
  SELECT r."year", res."driver_id", SUM(res."points") AS pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."driver_id"
),
driver_max AS (
  SELECT "year", MAX(pts) AS best_driver_pts
  FROM driver_totals
  GROUP BY "year"
)
SELECT *
FROM driver_max
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8. Constructor maxima per year (tidy CTE version)
WITH constructor_totals AS (
  SELECT r."year", res."constructor_id", SUM(res."points") AS pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."constructor_id"
),
constructor_max AS (
  SELECT "year", MAX(pts) AS best_constructor_pts
  FROM constructor_totals
  GROUP BY "year"
)
SELECT *
FROM constructor_max
ORDER BY "year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9. Year‑by‑year sum of (best driver pts + best constructor pts)
WITH driver_max AS (
  SELECT r."year", MAX(SUM(res."points")) AS best_driver_pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."driver_id"
),
constructor_max AS (
  SELECT r."year", MAX(SUM(res."points")) AS best_constructor_pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."constructor_id"
)
SELECT d."year",
       d.best_driver_pts,
       c.best_constructor_pts,
       d.best_driver_pts + c.best_constructor_pts AS combined_total
FROM driver_max AS d
JOIN constructor_max AS c ON c."year" = d."year"
ORDER BY d."year"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10. FINAL: the three seasons with the smallest combined total
WITH driver_max AS (
  SELECT r."year", MAX(SUM(res."points")) AS best_driver_pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."driver_id"
),
constructor_max AS (
  SELECT r."year", MAX(SUM(res."points")) AS best_constructor_pts
  FROM "results" AS res
  JOIN "races"  AS r ON r."race_id" = res."race_id"
  GROUP BY r."year", res."constructor_id"
),
combined AS (
  SELECT d."year",
         d.best_driver_pts + c.best_constructor_pts AS combined_total
  FROM driver_max AS d
  JOIN constructor_max AS c ON c."year" = d."year"
)
SELECT "year", combined_total
FROM combined
ORDER BY combined_total ASC, "year" ASC
LIMIT 3;
```

These ten queries gradually build up the logic and finally produce the three required years ordered by their (best driver + best constructor) combined points totals.
